    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Jackson Merrill** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt and a robust 13% boost from his platoon advantage. His ability to exploit Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which ranks in the 86th percentile for potential stolen base opportunities\u2014makes him an essential catalyst for our scarcity strategy. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an ideal scenario batting third against McGreevy; his 14% platoon edge is the highest among our starters, providing a clear path to both RBI and run accumulation. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a high-floor anchor at 74.07, as he should feast on Cristian Javier\u2019s porous 5.27 xERA, regardless of the pending confirmation of his second-spot placement.\n\nThe optimization process was tightest regarding **Cole Carrigg** (57.84), who narrowly missed the \"Strong\" start threshold. While his 14% park factor boost is enticing, the unfavorable matchup against the 3.49 xERA of Ian Seymour suppresses his ceiling, rendering him a marginal play best used only for specific categorical needs. Among our bench, we are currently navigating the absences of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Jordan Westburg**, all of whom are either on the IL or off today\u2019s slate. Consequently, there was no true \"bench dilemma\" today, as our active roster depth is fully deployed to combat the scarcity of stolen bases. We are monitoring lineup confirmations closely for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Cole Carrigg**; should any of these bats shift significantly down in the order, their efficiency scores will require re-evaluation before first pitch.",
